From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] arch_topology: multiply the capacity terms in 64 bits

topology_normalize_cpu_scale() multiplies a u32 capacity-dmips-mhz by
capacity_freq_ref, an unsigned long in kHz, and stores the product in a
u64; the multiplication itself is done in unsigned long, which is
32 bits on ARM32.  On the SM-T715 (Exynos5433, ARM32 kernel) the A57s'
3575 times 1 500 000 kHz is 5 362 500 000, which wraps to 1 067 532 704:
once the A57 table reached 1.5 GHz, the A57s got capacity 444 and the
A53s 1024, so the scheduler took the little cores for the big ones.  At
1.2 GHz the product, 4 290 000 000, was just under 2^32.

Cast the first factor to u64, as the destination already is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/base/arch_topology.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/base/arch_topology.c b/drivers/base/arch_topology.c
index 176429904..6158bb2cc 100644
--- a/drivers/base/arch_topology.c
+++ b/drivers/base/arch_topology.c
@@ -293,13 +293,13 @@ void topology_normalize_cpu_scale(void)
 
 	capacity_scale = 1;
 	for_each_possible_cpu(cpu) {
-		capacity = raw_capacity[cpu] * per_cpu(capacity_freq_ref, cpu);
+		capacity = (u64)raw_capacity[cpu] * per_cpu(capacity_freq_ref, cpu);
 		capacity_scale = max(capacity, capacity_scale);
 	}
 
 	pr_debug("cpu_capacity: capacity_scale=%llu\n", capacity_scale);
 	for_each_possible_cpu(cpu) {
-		capacity = raw_capacity[cpu] * per_cpu(capacity_freq_ref, cpu);
+		capacity = (u64)raw_capacity[cpu] * per_cpu(capacity_freq_ref, cpu);
 		capacity = div64_u64(capacity << SCHED_CAPACITY_SHIFT,
 			capacity_scale);
 		topology_set_cpu_scale(cpu, capacity);
-- 
